{"cut_proposal":{"candidate_errors":[],"prefix":"To solve for \\( x \\) that satisfies both equations \\( 18x^2 + 25x - 3 = 0 \\) and \\( 4x^2 + 8x + 3 = 0 \\), we will follow these steps:\n\n1. **Solve the quadratic equation \\( 4x^2 + 8x + 3 = 0 \\) for \\( x \\).**\n\nThe quadratic formula is given by:\n\\[\nx = \\frac{-b \\pm \\sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\n\\]\nFor the equation \\( 4x^2 + 8x + 3 = 0 \\), we have \\( a = 4 \\), \\( b = 8 \\), and \\( c = 3 \\).\n\nCalculate the discriminant:\n\\[\nb^2 - 4ac = 8^2 - 4 \\cdot 4 \\cdot 3 = 64 - 48 = 16\n\\]\n\nNow, apply the quadratic formula:\n\\[\nx = \\frac{-8 \\pm \\sqrt{16}}{2 \\cdot 4} = \\frac{-8 \\pm 4}{8}\n\\]\n\nThis gives us two solutions:\n\\[\nx = \\frac{-8 + 4}{8} = \\frac{-4}{8} = -\\frac{1}{2}\n\\]\n\\[\nx = \\frac{-8 - 4}{8} = \\frac{-12}{8} = -\\frac{3}{2}\n\\]\n\nSo, the solutions to \\( 4x^2 + 8x + 3 = 0 \\) are \\( x = -\\frac{1}{2} \\) and \\( x = -\\frac{3}{2} \\).\n\n2. **Check which of these solutions satisfy the equation \\( 18x^2 + 25x - 3 = 0 \\).**\n\n","prefix_end":903,"status":"review_required"},"eligible":false,"generation":{"generation":{"max_new_tokens":2048,"temperature":0.7,"top_k":0,"top_p":1.0},"ids":[1249,11625,369,17767,856,1124,8,429,67901,2176,37906,17767,220,16,23,87,61,17,488,220,17,20,87,481,220,18,284,220,15,1124,8,323,17767,220,19,87,61,17,488,220,23,87,488,220,18,284,220,15,1124,701,582,686,1795,1493,7354,1447,16,13,3070,50,3948,279,79151,23606,17767,220,19,87,61,17,488,220,23,87,488,220,18,284,220,15,1124,8,369,17767,856,1124,568,56177,785,79151,14806,374,2661,553,510,59,9640,87,284,1124,37018,19999,65,1124,5187,1124,26888,90,65,61,17,481,220,19,580,3417,90,17,64,532,59,921,2461,279,23606,17767,220,19,87,61,17,488,220,23,87,488,220,18,284,220,15,1124,701,582,614,17767,264,284,220,19,1124,701,17767,293,284,220,23,1124,701,323,17767,272,284,220,18,1124,3593,47866,279,49319,517,510,59,9640,65,61,17,481,220,19,580,284,220,23,61,17,481,220,19,1124,50853,220,19,1124,50853,220,18,2